---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CadenceTimeline from '../../components/CadenceTimeline.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Founder-led content and pipeline | Kadanco"
  description="A publishing motion in the founder's voice that feeds measurable pipeline. Messaging, ghostwriting, SEO and GEO, warmed outbound and the RevOps to track what converts, run by two operators."
>
  <main id="top">

    <!-- ===================== HERO ===================== -->
    <section class="hero" data-theme="dark">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow">Use case &middot; Founder-led content</span>
        <h1>Your point of view, published<br><span class="hl">until it produces pipeline.</span></h1>
        <p class="lead">Founders are the most credible voice a B2B company has, and the most starved for time. We turn your point of view into a publishing motion that runs every week without you writing it, and we track it through to pipeline instead of stopping at likes.</p>
        <div class="hero-cta">
          <button class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" data-open-modal>Get a free audit</button>
          <p class="hero-cta-note">We'll find the few things only you can say, then we publish them.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== WHY IT STALLS ===================== -->
    <section class="section band-paper" data-theme="light">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow dark">Why founder content stalls</span>
        <h2>Most founders start. <span class="hl-indigo">Few keep going.</span></h2>
        <div class="grid cols-3" style="margin-top:48px;text-align:left">
          <div class="card">
            <h3>It runs for a month</h3>
            <p>You post consistently until the first busy week. Then it stops, and the audience you were building forgets you.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>It gets likes, not meetings</h3>
            <p>Engagement looks healthy and nothing reaches the pipeline, because nobody connected the posts to the accounts you want.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>It stops sounding like you</h3>
            <p>Hand it to a junior or an agency and it flattens into marketing language. Buyers can tell, and credibility is the whole point.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== THE MOTION (loop) ===================== -->
    <section class="section" data-theme="light">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow indigo">How the motion works</span>
        <h2>A loop, <span class="hl-indigo">not a campaign.</span></h2>
        <p class="lead" style="margin-top:20px;max-width:740px">
          Your point of view goes out every week, the audience gets warmer, and what actually converts tells us what to write next.
        </p>
        <div style="max-width:1000px;margin:44px auto 0">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 1120 320" data-anim="diagram" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="width:100%;height:auto;display:block" role="img" aria-label="A loop: the founder's point of view is published every week, builds an audience that knows you, and produces pipeline you can trace. What converts feeds the next post.">
            <defs>
              <marker id="ucloopar" markerWidth="12" markerHeight="12" refX="7" refY="5" orient="auto" markerUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
                <path d="M1 1 L9 5 L1 9" fill="none" stroke="#3B38DF" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </marker>
            </defs>

            <rect x="20" y="40" width="240" height="92" rx="16" fill="#3B38DF"/>
            <text x="140" y="80" font-family="Fira Sans" font-size="17" font-weight="600" fill="#FFFFFF" text-anchor="middle">Your point</text>
            <text x="140" y="104" font-family="Fira Sans" font-size="17" font-weight="600" fill="#FFFFFF" text-anchor="middle">of view</text>

            <rect x="300" y="40" width="240" height="92" rx="16" fill="#FFFFFF" stroke="#E6E6F0" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <text x="420" y="80" font-family="Fira Sans" font-size="17" font-weight="500" fill="#201E1F" text-anchor="middle">Published</text>
            <text x="420" y="104" font-family="Fira Sans" font-size="17" font-weight="500" fill="#201E1F" text-anchor="middle">every week</text>

            <rect x="580" y="40" width="240" height="92" rx="16" fill="#FFFFFF" stroke="#E6E6F0" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <text x="700" y="80" font-family="Fira Sans" font-size="17" font-weight="500" fill="#201E1F" text-anchor="middle">An audience</text>
            <text x="700" y="104" font-family="Fira Sans" font-size="17" font-weight="500" fill="#201E1F" text-anchor="middle">that knows you</text>

            <rect x="860" y="40" width="240" height="92" rx="16" fill="#DAFF02"/>
            <text x="980" y="80" font-family="Fira Sans" font-size="17" font-weight="700" fill="#201E1F" text-anchor="middle">Pipeline</text>
            <text x="980" y="104" font-family="Fira Sans" font-size="17" font-weight="700" fill="#201E1F" text-anchor="middle">you can trace</text>

            <g fill="none" stroke="#3B38DF" stroke-width="2.5" marker-end="url(#ucloopar)">
              <path d="M260 86 L 292 86"/>
              <path d="M540 86 L 572 86"/>
              <path d="M820 86 L 852 86"/>
            </g>

            <path d="M980 132 L 980 240 Q 980 262 958 262 L 162 262 Q 140 262 140 240 L 140 140" fill="none" stroke="#B2B1FF" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="7 6" marker-end="url(#ucloopar)"/>
            <text x="560" y="292" font-family="Fira Sans" font-size="15" font-weight="500" fill="#5A5A72" text-anchor="middle">What converts tells us what to write next</text>
          </svg>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== WHAT WE RUN ===================== -->
    <section class="section band-deep" data-theme="dark">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow peri">What we run</span>
        <h2>Five workstreams, <span class="hl">one publishing motion.</span></h2>
        <div class="grid cols-3" style="margin-top:48px;text-align:left">
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Messaging and positioning</h3>
            <p>We find the few things only you can say, and the arguments worth repeating until the market remembers them.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Ghostwriting and content</h3>
            <p>Written in your voice from your thinking, not generic thought leadership. You approve, we publish.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>SEO and GEO</h3>
            <p>The same ideas built to be found in search and quoted by AI answers, so one interview earns traffic for months.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Outbound, warmed</h3>
            <p>Outreach that lands after the account has already seen you, so the first message is a continuation, not a cold open.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>RevOps that tracks it</h3>
            <p>Content tied to accounts, meetings and pipeline in your CRM, so you can see what produced revenue and what did not.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== WHAT YOU OWN ===================== -->
    <section class="section band-paper" data-theme="light">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="split">
          <div class="content">
            <span class="eyebrow indigo">What you own</span>
            <h2>A voice in the market, <span class="hl-indigo">and the pipeline to prove it.</span></h2>
          </div>
          <div class="content">
            <p class="lead">A publishing motion that runs every week in your voice, whether or not you had time that week. An audience that arrives at the sales call already knowing how you think. And a line you can follow from a post to a meeting to a deal, instead of a dashboard full of engagement you cannot bank.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== FIRST 90 DAYS ===================== -->
    <section class="section band-deep" data-theme="dark">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow peri">The first 90 days</span>
        <h2>Publishing in weeks, <span class="hl">not someday.</span></h2>
        <CadenceTimeline
          steps={[
            { n: "01", title: "Map", body: "We interview you properly, pull out the point of view you already have, and agree the arguments worth owning." },
            { n: "02", title: "Build", body: "We build the messaging, the content engine and the tracking, then write the first weeks ahead so the motion never depends on a free afternoon." },
            { n: "03", title: "Ship", amp: "& iterate", body: "You approve, we publish, every week. Then we read what converted and write more of it.", loop: "and the audience builds" },
          ]}
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== ONE USE CASE NOTE ===================== -->
    <section class="section center" data-theme="light">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="lead" style="max-width:720px;margin:0 auto">
          Founder-led content is one of the ways teams put Kadanco to work. It is one use case, not the whole offer. The same two operators run the full marketing function for B2B companies. <a class="hl-indigo" href="/">See how the full function works</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== FINAL CTA ===================== -->
    <section class="section cta-band center" data-theme="dark">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow peri">Lets Talk</span>
        <h2>Ready to <span class="hl">start publishing?</span></h2>
        <p class="lead" style="margin-top:20px">Tell us what you believe about your market. We'll turn it into a motion that runs every week.</p>
        <div class="cta-actions">
          <button class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" data-open-modal>Get a free audit</button>
        </div>
        <p class="cta-note">Free, no obligation. We'll get back to you quickly.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
</Layout>
